# 21. ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Before declaring the application complete, verify these real-world workflows:

TEST 1:
The trainer adds a member, uploads their photograph, sets a membership period, and records the package price.

The member receives an invitation and activates their account.

TEST 2:
The trainer assigns a workout plan.

The member logs in and sees the correct workout plan.

TEST 3:
The trainer assigns a diet plan containing several scheduled meals.

The member sees the assigned meals and records what they actually ate.

TEST 4:
The member uploads a meal photograph and submits a meal report.

The trainer can view the photograph, reported foods, quantities, and submission time.

TEST 5:
The member completes a workout and submits the exercise logs.

The trainer can review the report and see which exercises were completed.

TEST 6:
The trainer records a partial payment.

The system calculates the remaining balance correctly.

TEST 7:
A payment deadline passes without a full payment.

The system displays the correct outstanding balance and overdue status.

TEST 8:
The trainer publishes a notice for one specific member.

Only the intended recipient should receive and view the private notice.

TEST 9:
The trainer updates a diet plan.

The correct member sees the updated plan, while historical meal logs remain intact.

TEST 10:
A member attempts to access another member's profile or modify their payment status.

The backend must reject the unauthorized request.

TEST 11:
A scheduled workout or meal report is not submitted.

The system flags it as missing without incorrectly claiming that the member definitely skipped the activity.

TEST 12:
The trainer opens the dashboard on a phone, tablet, and desktop.

The layout remains functional, responsive, and visually polished.

